(6446030, 955267, 83026, '<td valign="top">Like everybody else, I was fooled.</td>', 'Like everybody else, I was fooled.', '2011-06-17 12:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446031, 955483, 83026, '<td valign="top">I remember seeing those skies when on a safari in the Serengeti. Thanks for bringing back those wonderful memories. It''s so difficult to see those kinds of skies these days with all the light pollution.</td>', 'I remember seeing those skies when on a safari in the Serengeti. Thanks for bringing back those wonderful memories. It''s so difficult to see those kinds of skies these days with all the light pollution.', '2011-06-17 12:36:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446036, 955267, 41337, '<td valign="top">I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that. <br/> <br/>Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion.</td>', 'I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that.  Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion.', '2011-06-17 12:51:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446093, 956184, 100831, '<td valign="top">what''s a snog? <br/>Must be lovely - and golden - and right.  <br/>I love this one!</td>', 'what''s a snog? Must be lovely - and golden - and right.  I love this one!', '2011-06-17 13:23:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446136, 955267, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that. <br/> <br/>Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do.</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that.  Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion.   Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do.', '2011-06-17 14:11:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446156, 955965, 30861, '<td valign="top">Got a 9 from me :-)</td>', 'Got a 9 from me :-)', '2011-06-17 14:30:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446206, 955267, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that. <br/> <br/>Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re not getting it. In most cases the viewer knows that fishing lines or something else is being used in the trick. The viewer knows that a trick is being done. In your case you''re attempting to pass off something as real when it wasn''t. If it was judged as the trick it was it would have scored 5.7 not 7.7. You know this. That''s why you called it "The Wild" and not the name of the statue.</td>', 'Originally posted by nightpixels: Originally posted by yanko: I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that.  Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion.   Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do.   You''re not getting it. In most cases the viewer knows that fishing lines or something else is being used in the trick. The viewer knows that a trick is being done. In your case you''re attempting to pass off something as real when it wasn''t. If it was judged as the trick it was it would have scored 5.7 not 7.7. You know this. That''s why you called it "The Wild" and not the name of the statue.', '2011-06-17 15:09:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446214, 955267, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that. <br/> <br/>Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re not getting it. In most cases the viewer knows that fishing lines or something else is being used in the trick. The viewer knows that a trick is being done. In your case you''re attempting to pass off something as real when it wasn''t. If it was judged as the trick it was it would have scored 5.7 not 7.7. You know this. That''s why you called it "The Wild" and not the name of the statue. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually it is YOU who is NOT getting it.  Where in the challenge did it say we are not allowed to photograph Silhouette of a statue???  show me!  It is none of your business if I choose to photograph a statue and also not of your business what I call it.  Get that through your thick skull, moron!</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Originally posted by nightpixels: Originally posted by yanko: I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that.  Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion.   Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do.   You''re not getting it. In most cases the viewer knows that fishing lines or something else is being used in the trick. The viewer knows that a trick is being done. In your case you''re attempting to pass off something as real when it wasn''t. If it was judged as the trick it was it would have scored 5.7 not 7.7. You know this. That''s why you called it "The Wild" and not the name of the statue.   Actually it is YOU who is NOT getting it.  Where in the challenge did it say we are not allowed to photograph Silhouette of a statue???  show me!  It is none of your business if I choose to photograph a statue and also not of your business what I call it.  Get that through your thick skull, moron!', '2011-06-17 15:16:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446221, 955267, 131377, '<td valign="top">I think many people knew this was a statue and still gave it a good vote. I could tell right away that the elk weren''t real, once I made the photo bigger. The lines are too smooth &amp; the elk are too dark in comparison with the rock for it to be real. Also... I mean, come on, look at them. They are all looking in different directions, some are moving and some are standing still. The bull is calling out but the does aren''t even paying attention, and those critters are loud. There was no trick here. It''s just a wonderful photo of a statue. What''s the big deal? I didn''t vote in this challenge, but if I had, I would have voted this up because of the quality of the photo itself, not the validity or realness of the elk.<br/> <br/>Well done, nightpixels. :) You earned a well-deserved ribbon.</td>', 'I think many people knew this was a statue and still gave it a good vote. I could tell right away that the elk weren''t real, once I made the photo bigger. The lines are too smooth & the elk are too dark in comparison with the rock for it to be real. Also... I mean, come on, look at them. They are all looking in different directions, some are moving and some are standing still. The bull is calling out but the does aren''t even paying attention, and those critters are loud. There was no trick here. It''s just a wonderful photo of a statue. What''s the big deal? I didn''t vote in this challenge, but if I had, I would have voted this up because of the quality of the photo itself, not the validity or realness of the elk. Well done, nightpixels. :) You earned a well-deserved ribbon.', '2011-06-17 15:34:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446223, 955267, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that. <br/> <br/>Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re not getting it. In most cases the viewer knows that fishing lines or something else is being used in the trick. The viewer knows that a trick is being done. In your case you''re attempting to pass off something as real when it wasn''t. If it was judged as the trick it was it would have scored 5.7 not 7.7. You know this. That''s why you called it "The Wild" and not the name of the statue. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually it is YOU who is NOT getting it.  Where in the challenge did it say we are not allowed to photograph Silhouette of a statue???  show me!  It is none of your business if I choose to photograph a statue and also not of your business what I call it.  Get that through your thick skull, moron! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Awesome.</td>', 'Originally posted by nightpixels: Originally posted by yanko: Originally posted by nightpixels: Originally posted by yanko: I''m glad I didn''t vote in this challenge because I would have been very disappointed to learn that this was just a statue. You''re a good photographer, but it looks like you''re letting the ribbon chase get in the way of the making honest to good photographs. Even as someone who use to compete in the ribbon chase this feels cheap. You''re much better thant that.  Anyway, dismiss this if you like. Just one man''s opinion.   Not sure what you mean.  It was a Silhouette challenge and nowhere it said I cannot photograph a statue.  Then I guess you can make the same argument about people who use fishing lines to come up with photographs that look "deceiving" which is something I never do.   You''re not getting it. In most cases the viewer knows that fishing lines or something else is being used in the trick. The viewer knows that a trick is being done. In your case you''re attempting to pass off something as real when it wasn''t. If it was judged as the trick it was it would have scored 5.7 not 7.7. You know this. That''s why you called it "The Wild" and not the name of the statue.   Actually it is YOU who is NOT getting it.  Where in the challenge did it say we are not allowed to photograph Silhouette of a statue???  show me!  It is none of your business if I choose to photograph a statue and also not of your business what I call it.  Get that through your thick skull, moron!   Awesome.', '2011-06-17 15:41:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446255, 955483, 50695, '<td valign="top">wow, a red ribbon and you didn''t even have to take your hands out of your pockets....<br/> <br/>a 6 from me, amazing shot.</td>', 'wow, a red ribbon and you didn''t even have to take your hands out of your pockets.... a 6 from me, amazing shot.', '2011-06-17 16:45:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446258, 955267, 124255, '<td valign="top">nice!  I didn''t vote but just checked it out. I knew something was wrong because you don''t see bulls with cows this time of year- thought at first it was a date violation but since it was a legal date - more power too you. I''ve seen a lot more leeway with the rules on challenges than this photo - OK in my book<br/></td>', 'nice!  I didn''t vote but just checked it out. I knew something was wrong because you don''t see bulls with cows this time of year- thought at first it was a date violation but since it was a legal date - more power too you. I''ve seen a lot more leeway with the rules on challenges than this photo - OK in my book', '2011-06-17 16:49:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446259, 956295, 50695, '<td valign="top">beautiful fro. 7 from me.</td>', 'beautiful fro. 7 from me.', '2011-06-17 16:49:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446260, 956317, 50695, '<td valign="top">intriguing found sculpture. my kind of art. 7 from me.</td>', 'intriguing found sculpture. my kind of art. 7 from me.', '2011-06-17 16:49:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446261, 955323, 50695, '<td valign="top">fascinating effect. 7 from me.</td>', 'fascinating effect. 7 from me.', '2011-06-17 16:50:19.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6446264, 956319, 50695, '<td valign="top">well done. 7 from me.</td>', 'well done. 7 from me.', '2011-06-17 16:52:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446266, 956261, 50695, '<td valign="top">that flying bird seems strangely out of place. I gave you a 7.</td>', 'that flying bird seems strangely out of place. I gave you a 7.', '2011-06-17 16:53:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446267, 956324, 50695, '<td valign="top">love this composition. 7 from me.</td>', 'love this composition. 7 from me.', '2011-06-17 16:53:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446269, 956319, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by clive_patric_nolan:</b></div><hr/><i> Fantastic how you''ve brought these to life.  In my top ten of the challenge. 9. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Most silhouettes that do well in these challenges tend to be static and lifeless. They often get by on color and sharpeness alone. Sometimes the subjects are asked to jump in an attempt to make the image come alive, which is what a photograph really needs. Here, the subjects aren''t even alive much less jumping around yet this is more real than many other photos depicting real subjects. A credit to the photographer.</td>', 'Originally posted by clive_patric_nolan: Fantastic how you''ve brought these to life.  In my top ten of the challenge. 9.   Most silhouettes that do well in these challenges tend to be static and lifeless. They often get by on color and sharpeness alone. Sometimes the subjects are asked to jump in an attempt to make the image come alive, which is what a photograph really needs. Here, the subjects aren''t even alive much less jumping around yet this is more real than many other photos depicting real subjects. A credit to the photographer.', '2011-06-17 16:53:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446270, 956268, 50695, '<td valign="top">voyeuristic. fascinating. disturbing. I gave this a 7, which is as high as I went in this challenge.</td>', 'voyeuristic. fascinating. disturbing. I gave this a 7, which is as high as I went in this challenge.', '2011-06-17 16:54:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446271, 955323, 41337, '<td valign="top">The composition seems after the fact, but you can''t beat that energy.</td>', 'The composition seems after the fact, but you can''t beat that energy.', '2011-06-17 16:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446279, 955629, 50695, '<td valign="top">beautiful brutal blur. 7 from me. (I quit at 7 for this challenge)</td>', 'beautiful brutal blur. 7 from me. (I quit at 7 for this challenge)', '2011-06-17 17:01:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446280, 955629, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jamesgoss:</b></div><hr/><i>a bit too much recognizable form to be "abstract", yet at the same time, a bit too much abstractness to fall within the portrait realm.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>that''s what makes it so good. funny how people need categories.</td>', 'Originally posted by jamesgoss:a bit too much recognizable form to be "abstract", yet at the same time, a bit too much abstractness to fall within the portrait realm.  that''s what makes it so good. funny how people need categories.', '2011-06-17 17:02:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446283, 955784, 50695, '<td valign="top">Freudian masterpiece. Welcome to high modernism. :)</td>', 'Freudian masterpiece. Welcome to high modernism. :)', '2011-06-17 17:04:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446284, 956136, 50695, '<td valign="top">7 from me. Great color and composition.</td>', '7 from me. Great color and composition.', '2011-06-17 17:04:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446292, 956136, 62357, '<td valign="top">Something about this just works for me.  Sorry you didn''t do better.</td>', 'Something about this just works for me.  Sorry you didn''t do better.', '2011-06-17 17:17:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446304, 955267, 86958, '<td valign="top">Statue or not - this is a great image! The highest score I''ve given any photo.</td>', 'Statue or not - this is a great image! The highest score I''ve given any photo.', '2011-06-17 17:49:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446305, 956184, 23484, '<td valign="top">Absolutely amazing shot. should have been number 1.</td>', 'Absolutely amazing shot. should have been number 1.', '2011-06-17 17:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446315, 955267, 115307, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon!<br/>I''ll admit I was a bit dissapointed that this isn''t real. Not because it decreases the quality of the photograph (because this is still absolutely fantastic) but because it greatly decreases the difficulty level of obtaining the shot, and to me that matters when considering how impressed I am by a photo.<br/>Cheers on the nevertheless fantastic photograph</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon!I''ll admit I was a bit dissapointed that this isn''t real. Not because it decreases the quality of the photograph (because this is still absolutely fantastic) but because it greatly decreases the difficulty level of obtaining the shot, and to me that matters when considering how impressed I am by a photo.Cheers on the nevertheless fantastic photograph', '2011-06-17 18:18:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446352, 956052, 120129, '<td valign="top">I just wanna know where you go to get a personal hot shot fireman?!?! Oh and congrats on your ribbon and beautiful work. ;)</td>', 'I just wanna know where you go to get a personal hot shot fireman?!?! Oh and congrats on your ribbon and beautiful work. ;)', '2011-06-17 19:34:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446371, 956320, 47470, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe this didn''t even break a 6!  Completely underrated.</td>', 'I can''t believe this didn''t even break a 6!  Completely underrated.', '2011-06-17 20:37:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446379, 955483, 132967, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  Great capture!</td>', 'Beautiful!  Great capture!', '2011-06-17 21:12:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446405, 956322, 100831, '<td valign="top">7 from me. I really like the light. Congrats on the TT. Great job.</td>', '7 from me. I really like the light. Congrats on the TT. Great job.', '2011-06-17 22:01:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446409, 955267, 86447, '<td valign="top">I don''t mind at all the difficulty or easiness of obtaining an image.    What matters is the image (to me).    An image is only what it appears to be ... and nothing else.  <br/> <br/>It only can stand upon what it shows the viewer.<br/> <br/>And... you''ve shown us a magnificent silhouette shot.<br/> <br/>Kudos to you and congrats on your ribbon!<br/></td>', 'I don''t mind at all the difficulty or easiness of obtaining an image.    What matters is the image (to me).    An image is only what it appears to be ... and nothing else.   It only can stand upon what it shows the viewer. And... you''ve shown us a magnificent silhouette shot. Kudos to you and congrats on your ribbon!', '2011-06-17 22:14:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446435, 955483, 86447, '<td valign="top">Fabulous!  Congrats on the moment... and on the capture.<br/> <br/>Oh  yeah... and the ribbon!  :)<br/></td>', 'Fabulous!  Congrats on the moment... and on the capture. Oh  yeah... and the ribbon!  :)', '2011-06-17 23:30:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446436, 956052, 86447, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Juliet (again... and again ... and again recently).  :)<br/></td>', 'Congrats, Juliet (again... and again ... and again recently).  :)', '2011-06-17 23:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446438, 956184, 86447, '<td valign="top">What a romantic and beautiful scene.</td>', 'What a romantic and beautiful scene.', '2011-06-17 23:32:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446439, 956265, 86447, '<td valign="top">Fabulous collection of silhouettes!</td>', 'Fabulous collection of silhouettes!', '2011-06-17 23:32:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446440, 956323, 86447, '<td valign="top">Perfect for the challenge...  But, I''m not seeing the bat.    But, I''m old... LOL!</td>', 'Perfect for the challenge...  But, I''m not seeing the bat.    But, I''m old... LOL!', '2011-06-17 23:33:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446441, 956322, 86447, '<td valign="top">Lovely.</td>', 'Lovely.', '2011-06-17 23:33:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446502, 955396, 80831, '<td valign="top">Scripps pier?</td>', 'Scripps pier?', '2011-06-18 01:08:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446514, 955396, 65319, '<td valign="top">Jenn...is this a self-portrait?  Is that you in the photo?  I like the moodiness of this photo...the thoughtful pose of the person and the dimensional echoes of the pier squares.  The focus appears a bit soft for my taste and the heavy frame feels claustrophobic in a photo that demands breathing space.  Beautiful location!</td>', 'Jenn...is this a self-portrait?  Is that you in the photo?  I like the moodiness of this photo...the thoughtful pose of the person and the dimensional echoes of the pier squares.  The focus appears a bit soft for my taste and the heavy frame feels claustrophobic in a photo that demands breathing space.  Beautiful location!', '2011-06-18 01:52:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446515, 955267, 62727, '<td valign="top">I was hoping this was a shot of some real elk, and was a little disappointed that it''s not. But it''s okay with me that it''s a statue. It''s an awesome shot either way. I gave you one of those 10s. Congrats!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-18 00:53:59.</i></td>', 'I was hoping this was a shot of some real elk, and was a little disappointed that it''s not. But it''s okay with me that it''s a statue. It''s an awesome shot either way. I gave you one of those 10s. Congrats!', '2011-06-18 01:53:23.000000', '2011-06-18 01:53:59.000000', 0),
(6446520, 955267, 39057, '<td valign="top">I thought this was real until I came to look over the shot and read the description.</td>', 'I thought this was real until I came to look over the shot and read the description.', '2011-06-18 02:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446522, 955483, 39057, '<td valign="top">This was my pick for blue. I can''t believe that you live in a place where a 30 sec exposure can show all those stars!<br/></td>', 'This was my pick for blue. I can''t believe that you live in a place where a 30 sec exposure can show all those stars!', '2011-06-18 02:21:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446523, 955483, 39057, '<td valign="top">LOL....Looks like I was duped by the blue winner !<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> Well ...went through 5 shots and this is the best so far ! I hope I''m not being duped by a cut out figure pasted on a computer screen ! </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'LOL....Looks like I was duped by the blue winner ! Originally posted by kenskid: Well ...went through 5 shots and this is the best so far ! I hope I''m not being duped by a cut out figure pasted on a computer screen ! ', '2011-06-18 02:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446547, 955267, 17186, '<td valign="top">Ha! Interesting comments. For me, the plaque on the lower right portion of the rock served as more than adequate notice that I was viewing a very nice picture of statuary. Of the many elk that loiter in my neighborhood I have never seen any of them standing on a rock with a plaque! I guess not seeing detail in the scene one is viewing is how an illusion is created. If it fooled you and you feel duped, it should be a good reminder to look more closely at the scene you are critiquing, lest you play the fool (the role that is probably upsetting some.) Still the best photo in the challenge!</td>', 'Ha! Interesting comments. For me, the plaque on the lower right portion of the rock served as more than adequate notice that I was viewing a very nice picture of statuary. Of the many elk that loiter in my neighborhood I have never seen any of them standing on a rock with a plaque! I guess not seeing detail in the scene one is viewing is how an illusion is created. If it fooled you and you feel duped, it should be a good reminder to look more closely at the scene you are critiquing, lest you play the fool (the role that is probably upsetting some.) Still the best photo in the challenge!', '2011-06-18 04:38:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446551, 955483, 114565, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot, I absolutely love it.<br/>Shoot the person who gave you a vote of 3, they just dont appreciate the wonder that it space!</td>', 'Fantastic shot, I absolutely love it.Shoot the person who gave you a vote of 3, they just dont appreciate the wonder that it space!', '2011-06-18 04:44:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446555, 955267, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by xakpeet:</b></div><hr/><i> Ha! Interesting comments. For me, the plaque on the lower right portion of the rock served as more than adequate notice that I was viewing a very nice picture of statuary. Of the many elk that loiter in my neighborhood I have never seen any of them standing on a rock with a plaque! I guess not seeing detail in the scene one is viewing is how an illusion is created. If it fooled you and you feel duped, it should be a good reminder to look more closely at the scene you are critiquing, lest you play the fool (the role that is probably upsetting some.) Still the best photo in the challenge! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good point on the plaque in the lower right.  I could have removed it but chose not to so that people who look closely would see that this is in fact a statue.</td>', 'Originally posted by xakpeet: Ha! Interesting comments. For me, the plaque on the lower right portion of the rock served as more than adequate notice that I was viewing a very nice picture of statuary. Of the many elk that loiter in my neighborhood I have never seen any of them standing on a rock with a plaque! I guess not seeing detail in the scene one is viewing is how an illusion is created. If it fooled you and you feel duped, it should be a good reminder to look more closely at the scene you are critiquing, lest you play the fool (the role that is probably upsetting some.) Still the best photo in the challenge!   Good point on the plaque in the lower right.  I could have removed it but chose not to so that people who look closely would see that this is in fact a statue.', '2011-06-18 04:50:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446559, 956195, 131284, '<td valign="top">Nice, just a shame about the lens flare on the subjects left sleeve. You said you''re not too familiar with post processing, so fyi that can be easily removed with the ''spot removal'' tool in lightroom or the ''spot healing brush'' in photoshop.</td>', 'Nice, just a shame about the lens flare on the subjects left sleeve. You said you''re not too familiar with post processing, so fyi that can be easily removed with the ''spot removal'' tool in lightroom or the ''spot healing brush'' in photoshop.', '2011-06-18 06:00:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446570, 956052, 34192, '<td valign="top">beautiful!<br/>Congrats!</td>', 'beautiful!Congrats!', '2011-06-18 08:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446574, 956052, 33182, '<td valign="top">So...this explains what you''ve been doing instead of being on facebook!!! Congrats!!!</td>', 'So...this explains what you''ve been doing instead of being on facebook!!! Congrats!!!', '2011-06-18 09:11:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446587, 956265, 101702, '<td valign="top">This was my pick for the blue, I was one of your 9''s. Fantastically moody image, with great tones and movement.</td>', 'This was my pick for the blue, I was one of your 9''s. Fantastically moody image, with great tones and movement.', '2011-06-18 10:04:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446628, 955267, 131377, '<td valign="top">Oh wow, I didn''t even see the plaque until you guys mentioned it. That settles the "dirty trick" argument quite well. ;)</td>', 'Oh wow, I didn''t even see the plaque until you guys mentioned it. That settles the "dirty trick" argument quite well. ;)', '2011-06-18 10:42:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446643, 955965, 101702, '<td valign="top">Interesting... I have no vote registered on this one, but voted 100% on the challenge. Presumably this was DQ''d during the voting stage, but this means that should you now be validated, you may have unfairly missed out on some votes - albeit I guess that could have worked either way. I probably would have given this a 6 or a 7 (would have to see it in context with all my other votes to determine which and that''s sadly not possible now). Had I given a 6 you are better off without my vote as it was below your average. Had I given a 7 you have lost out as it would have bumped you up a bit. Of course there may have been some more 7-10 votes heading your way that you never got :-/<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-18 10:05:51.</i></td>', 'Interesting... I have no vote registered on this one, but voted 100% on the challenge. Presumably this was DQ''d during the voting stage, but this means that should you now be validated, you may have unfairly missed out on some votes - albeit I guess that could have worked either way. I probably would have given this a 6 or a 7 (would have to see it in context with all my other votes to determine which and that''s sadly not possible now). Had I given a 6 you are better off without my vote as it was below your average. Had I given a 7 you have lost out as it would have bumped you up a bit. Of course there may have been some more 7-10 votes heading your way that you never got :-/', '2011-06-18 11:05:26.000000', '2011-06-18 11:05:51.000000', 0),
(6446728, 955267, 97166, '<td valign="top">All I can do is laugh at people that feel disappointed or tricked by something like this.  A little too much time on their hands. It''s amusing.</td>', 'All I can do is laugh at people that feel disappointed or tricked by something like this.  A little too much time on their hands. It''s amusing.', '2011-06-18 15:02:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6446734, 955483, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> LOL....Looks like I was duped by the blue winner !<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> Well ...went through 5 shots and this is the best so far ! I hope I''m not being duped by a cut out figure pasted on a computer screen ! </i></td></tr></table> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Dishonesty isn''t scooter88''s style. But if that were to change, I''ve heard all you need to do to sleep well at night is to leave a tiny sign in the photo but be sure to make it so that it''s 99% black with a font size of .01 microns.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-18 14:17:13.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kenskid: LOL....Looks like I was duped by the blue winner ! Originally posted by kenskid: Well ...went through 5 shots and this is the best so far ! I hope I''m not being duped by a cut out figure pasted on a computer screen !    Dishonesty isn''t scooter88''s style. But if that were to change, I''ve heard all you need to do to sleep well at night is to leave a tiny sign in the photo but be sure to make it so that it''s 99% black with a font size of .01 microns.', '2011-06-18 15:16:30.000000', '2011-06-18 15:17:13.000000', 0),
(6446795, 955267, 115307, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K10DGuy:</b></div><hr/><i> All I can do is laugh at people that feel disappointed or tricked by something like this.  A little too much time on their hands. It''s amusing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It doesn''t take time to feel tricked or disappointed, it happens in an instance, a gut reaction :-)<br/>And neither is such a feeling a bad thing. My reaction to reading the description was "Aww man, its not real, that would have been SO cool if it was real". Its not going into a rage, and it isn''t devalueing the photograph either.<br/>This is still hands down the best photo in the challenge and it deserves the ribbon. If it had been real, it would have been a miracle shot and just that tiny bit cooler as a result.</td>', 'Originally posted by K10DGuy: All I can do is laugh at people that feel disappointed or tricked by something like this.  A little too much time on their hands. It''s amusing.   It doesn''t take time to feel tricked or disappointed, it happens in an instance, a gut reaction :-)And neither is such a feeling a bad thing. My reaction to reading the description was "Aww man, its not real, that would have been SO cool if it was real". Its not going into a rage, and it isn''t devalueing the photograph either.This is still hands down the best photo in the challenge and it deserves the ribbon. If it had been real, it would have been a miracle shot and just that tiny bit cooler as a result.', '2011-06-18 17:55:26.000000', NULL, 0),
